AffiTox
=======

This repository is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). MIT covers
AffiTox source code, pipeline wrappers, and original curation/analysis scripts.

Third-party data, model weights, and docking binaries are **not** covered by
MIT. Redistribute them only under their original terms. The CC BY 4.0 license
on Zenodo data records applies to AffiTox organization, derived tables, and
figures. Mirrored ChEMBL extracts, PDB files, and method checkpoints remain
subject to the licenses below.

Datasets
--------
- ChEMBL (EMBL-EBI). Primary experimental Ki source for this release.
  Zdrazil et al., Nucleic Acids Research (2024).
  https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/
  https://chembl.gitbook.io/chembl-interface-documentation/about
  Use of ChEMBL data must follow EMBL-EBI terms (typically CC BY-SA 3.0 for
  ChEMBL data dumps). Do not re-license ChEMBL tables as MIT.
- RCSB PDB / wwPDB structures in input/proteins/.
  https://www.rcsb.org/
  https://www.rcsb.org/pages/policies
  https://www.wwpdb.org/documentation/policy
- BindingDB dumps may exist under input/bindingdb/ as provenance only and are
  **not** the public layer-1 source. Liu et al., Nucleic Acids Research (2007).
  https://www.bindingdb.org/

Evaluated methods (install separately; docs/INSTALL.md, docs/SOFTWARE_REGISTRY.md)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- QVina2 (QuickVina 2). Alhossary et al., Bioinformatics (2015).
  https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btv082
- GNINA 1.3. McNutt et al., Journal of Cheminformatics (2021).
  https://doi.org/10.1186/s13321-021-00522-2
  https://github.com/gnina/gnina
- DynamicBind. Lu et al., Nature Communications (2024).
  https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-45461-2
  https://github.com/luwei0917/DynamicBind
- Boltz-2. Passaro et al., bioRxiv (2025).
  https://doi.org/10.1101/2025.06.14.659707
  https://github.com/jwohlwend/boltz
- PLAPT / WELP-PLAPT.
  https://github.com/trrt-good/WELP-PLAPT
- PoseBusters. Buttenschoen, Morris, Deane, Chemical Science (2024).
  https://doi.org/10.1039/D3SC04185A
  https://github.com/maabuu/posebusters
  (PoseBusters is excluded for PLAPT, which does not generate poses.)

